<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Midas raises yr headline shr, div.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Midas raises yr headline shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		87.1	  vs   84.7</p>
<p>    - attrib		  89.7	  vs   86.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 26.0	  vs   21.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   14.76	 vs   14.17</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   19.03	 vs   13.98</p>
<p>    Tax			  4.27	 vs    0.43</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    4.98	 vs    8.84</p>
<p>    Turnover		 409.70	 vs  405.99</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	0.76	 vs    1.74</p>
<p>Div payable: Sept 12</p>
<p>On register: Sept 30</p>
<p>Full name: Midas Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it had acquired three companies for 13 million rand: the two branches of Queen Motor Spares in East London and King Williamstown with effect from March 1 1997; an 85 percent interest in specialist exhaust distributor Sten Distribution with effect from July 1; and a 50 percent interest in franchised fitment chain Auto 911 with effect from July 1.</p>
<p>The company said that it was well placed to increase market share in targeted growth sectors.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
<p>	 e-mail: johannesburg.newsroom@reuters.com</p>
